ct': {\n            'id': '2-2',\n            ...\n```\n\nHmm, actually I recall the test:\n\n```python\n    _TESTS = [{\n        'url': 'https://linuxacademy.com/cp/courses/lesson/course/1498/chapter/2/lesson/2',\n        'md5': '...',\n        'info_dict': {\n            'id': '2-2',\n            'ext': 'mp4',\n            'title': \"Introduction\",\n            ...\n```\n\nWait, but that URL contains 'course/1498' \u2014 would course_id be 1498? Then item_id would be '1498' and it'd be the course path... Hmm, but the test expects a single video with id '2-2'. Let me think.\n\nActually I think the _VALID_URL is:\n\n```python\n    _VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n                    https?://\n                        (?:\n                            |\n                            (?P<course_id>\\d+)\n                        )\n                    '''\n```\n\nHmm no. Let me look at the actual youtube-dl code. I remember the linuxacademy extractor was added in 2019. Let me recall:\n\n```python\nclass LinuxAcademyIE(InfoExtractor):\n    _VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n                    https?://\n                        (?:\n                            |\n                            (?P<course_id>\\d+)\n                        )\n                    '''\n```\n\nI clearly don't remember. The get_info tool should tell me. Let me just call it.\n\nActually, from the code snippet given in the problem: `mobj.group('chapter_id', 'lesson_id', 'course_id')` and `item_id = course_id if course_id else '%s-%s' % (chapter_id, lecture_id)`. So the URL groups are chapter_id, lesson_id, course_id.\n\nThe real _VALID_URL from youtube-dl:\n\n```python\n    _VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n                    https?://\n                        (?:\n                            |\n                            (?P<course_id>\\d+)\n                        )\n                    '''\n```\n\nOK, enough. I'll call get_info('LinuxAcademyIE._VALID_URL') and get_info('LinuxAcademyIE').\n\nLet me also verify helper functions