eally need to check. Let me use the get_info tool with name 'LinuxAcademyIE._VALID_URL' or 'LinuxAcademyIE'.\n\nActually the tool says: \"Returns information about a symbol.\" with name like 'f' for function f or 'C.foo' for method foo. So I can try 'LinuxAcademyIE' and 'LinuxAcademyIE._VALID_URL'.\n\nLet me plan the calls:\n1. `get_info('LinuxAcademyIE')` \u2014 get class info.\n2. `get_info('LinuxAcademyIE._VALID_URL')` \u2014 get the regex.\n3. Maybe `get_info('LinuxAcademyIE._real_extract')`.\n\nThese are independent, so I can call them all at once.\n\nThen write the tests.\n\nLet me draft the test file:\n\n```python\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.extractor.linuxacademy import LinuxAcademyIE\n\n\nCOURSE_URL = 'https://linuxacademy.com/cp/courses/lesson/course/1498/chapter/2/lesson/2'\nLESSON_URL = 'https://linuxacademy.com/lesson/lesson/2152'\n\n\ndef _make_ie():\n    return LinuxAcademyIE()\n\n\ndef test_course_path(monkeypatch):\n    ie = LinuxAcademyIE()\n\n    webpage = u'''\n    <html><head><title>Course</title></head><body>\n    window.module = {\n        \"title\": \"Test Course\",\n        \"md_desc\": \"Course md description\",\n        \"duration\": \"1 hour\",\n        \"items\": [\n            \"not-a-dict\",\n            {\"type\": {\"name\": \"Section\", \"slug\": \"section\"},\n             \"course_name\": \"Chapter One\", \"course_module\": \"mod-1\"},\n            {\"type\": {\"name\": \"Lesson\", \"slug\": \"lesson\"},\n             \"url\": \"/lesson/lesson/2152\",\n             \"title\": \"Lesson One\",\n             \"md_desc\": \"Lesson one description\",\n             \"date\": \"2019-01-01T10:00:00Z\",\n             \"duration\": \"5 min\"},\n            {\"type\": {\"name\": \"Quiz\", \"slug\": \"quiz\"}},\n            {\"type\": {\"name\": \"Lesson\", \"slug\": \"lesson\"}},\n            {\"type\": {\"name\": \"Lesson\", \"slug\": \"lesson\"},\n             \"url\": \"https://linuxacademy.com/lesson/lesson/