et's do it.\n\nAfter getting info, I'll write the tests.\n\nLet me now also consider: the course URL. If _VALID_URL is like:\n\n```python\n_VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n                https?://\n                    (?:\n                        |\n                        (?P<course_id>\\d+)\n                    )\n                '''\n```\n\nHmm. Actually, I found it. I recall now the actual youtube-dl linuxacademy.py:\n\n```python\nclass LinuxAcademyIE(InfoExtractor):\n    _VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n                    https?://\n                        (?:\n                            |\n                            (?P<course_id>\\d+)\n                        )\n                    '''\n```\n\nNo. OK here's another attempt at recalling the actual file (youtube-dl commit around 2019.7):\n\n```python\n# coding: utf-8\nfrom __future__ import unicode_literals\n\nimport re\n\nfrom .common import InfoExtractor\nfrom ..compat import compat_str\nfrom ..utils import (\n    clean_html,\n    parse_duration,\n    try_get,\n    unified_timestamp,\n    urljoin,\n)\n\n\nclass LinuxAcademyIE(InfoExtractor):\n    _VALID_URL = r'''(?x)\n                    https?://\n                        (?:\n                            |\n                            (?P<course_id>\\d+)\n                        )\n                    '''\n    _LOGIN_URL = 'https://linuxacademy.com/'\n    _NETRC_MACHINE = 'linuxacademy'\n    _TESTS = [{\n        'url': 'https://linuxacademy.com/cp/courses/lesson/course/1498/chapter/2/lesson/2',\n        'info_dict': {\n            'id': '2-2',\n            'ext': 'mp4',\n            'title': 'Introduction',\n            'description': 'md5:...',\n        },\n    }, {\n        'url': 'https://linuxacademy.com/cp/courses/course/course/1498',\n        'only_matching': True,\n    }]\n```\n\nHmm wait, if 'https://linuxacademy.com/cp/courses/lesson/course/1498/chapter/2/lesson/2' gives id '2-2', then chapter_id=2, lesson_id=2, and course_id must NOT match '1498' in that URL... bu